WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.124
Bobby could find only one item on Aunt Martha's list: tomato soup.

2
00:00:06.125 --> 00:00:08.158
He took it to the counter.

3
00:00:08.159 --> 00:00:11.960
Mr. Keefer peered at him from behind thick glasses.

4
00:00:11.961 --> 00:00:17.894
Bobby tried to smile, but being a shy boy, he felt very uncomfortable.

5
00:00:17.895 --> 00:00:20.895
Jane was the most outgoing of the children.

6
00:00:20.896 --> 00:00:23.785
She smiled and talked to everyone.

7
00:00:23.786 --> 00:00:28.778
Bobby noticed colorful balloons tied to a teddy bear on the counter.

8
00:00:28.779 --> 00:00:32.267
"How much for a balloon?" he asked.

9
00:00:32.268 --> 00:00:37.438
Lamb loved to play with balloons, so Bobby wanted to get him some.

10
00:00:37.439 --> 00:00:41.099
"Twenty-five cents," replied Mr. Keefer.

11
00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:46.416
"I'll take two," Bobby said as he counted out the money.

12
00:00:46.417 --> 00:00:49.014
"Aren't you a little old for that?"

13
00:00:49.015 --> 00:00:51.637
Aunt Martha said from behind.

14
00:00:51.638 --> 00:00:56.642
"Not for me," giggled Bobby, "for Lamb."

15
00:00:56.643 --> 00:01:00.418
Aunt Martha gave Bobby a strange look.

16
00:01:00.419 --> 00:01:02.648
"Who?" she asked.

17
00:01:02.649 --> 00:01:04.168
"For the bab . . . ,"

18
00:01:04.169 --> 00:01:08.830
Bobby began before he realized that there was no Lamb.

19
00:01:08.831 --> 00:01:14.597
"Uh, nothing. Maybe I won't take them," he said quickly.

20
00:01:14.598 --> 00:01:19.575
For some reason, Bobby suddenly felt like crying.

21
00:01:19.576 --> 00:01:21.985
"Do you want a candy?"

22
00:01:21.986 --> 00:01:25.729
Mr. Keefer held out a jar full of colored sweets.

23
00:01:25.730 --> 00:01:27.992
Bobby carefully took one.

24
00:01:27.993 --> 00:01:32.459
"Go on," Mr. Keefer said, "take more."

25
00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:37.489
Usually Bobby had to share everything with his brother and sisters.

26
00:01:37.490 --> 00:01:41.273
Since he was alone now, he could have more of everything.

27
00:01:41.274 --> 00:01:45.047
Happily, Bobby grabbed a handful of candies.

28
00:01:45.048 --> 00:01:51.217
Aunt Martha was upset that Bobby had not helped more with the shopping.

29
00:01:51.218 --> 00:01:57.111
Still, she made him his favorite sandwich before leaving to meet her friend.

30
00:01:57.112 --> 00:02:04.591
Even though Bobby loved peanut butter and pickle sandwiches, it was no fun to eat this snack alone.

31
00:02:04.592 --> 00:02:10.449
The silence around him was making him sad, so he went outside.

32
00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:15.828
He picked up a soccer ball, but there was nobody to play with.

33
00:02:15.829 --> 00:02:20.707
He got on his bike, but it was no fun riding by himself.

34
00:02:20.708 --> 00:02:24.516
He looked up at the bright sunny sky.

35
00:02:24.517 --> 00:02:28.803
"How long before the sun sets?" he wondered.

36
00:02:28.804 --> 00:02:32.152
The day seemed to be unusually long.

37
00:02:32.153 --> 00:02:37.649
Bobby thought very hard of all the bad things his brother and sisters did to him.

38
00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:41.286
He tried to act as if he didn't miss his siblings.

39
00:02:41.287 --> 00:02:45.458
"Cy always teases me," he said aloud.

40
00:02:45.459 --> 00:02:48.123
"Jane always screams.

41
00:02:48.124 --> 00:02:51.472
Panther acts like she's the boss.

42
00:02:51.473 --> 00:02:54.490
Lamb cries all the time."

43
00:02:54.491 --> 00:02:58.524
But the truth was, he missed them terribly.

44
00:02:58.525 --> 00:03:02.214
Then a horrible thought entered his head.

45
00:03:02.215 --> 00:03:06.965
What if he never saw Cy or Panther or Jane or Lamb again?

46
00:03:06.966 --> 00:03:10.698
Bobby's heart began to thump loudly.

47
00:03:10.699 --> 00:03:16.636
"What if Huey is gone and my wish will never be undone?" he said.

48
00:03:16.637 --> 00:03:24.088
Too scared to say anything more, Bobby ran as fast as he could through the woods.

49
00:03:24.089 --> 00:03:28.138
He reached Huey's well and tried to pull the bucket up.

50
00:03:28.139 --> 00:03:32.754
"Huey! Huey! I've changed my mind!"

51
00:03:32.755 --> 00:03:36.402
Bobby cried, pulling with all his might.

52
00:03:36.403 --> 00:03:40.154
For some reason, the bucket would not move.

53
00:03:40.155 --> 00:03:50.142
"No! No!" screamed Bobby, but the rope remained stiff, and the bucket stuck firmly to the bottom of the well.

54
00:03:50.143 --> 00:03:55.597
Bobby fell to the ground, crying, afraid, and very much alone.

55
00:03:55.598 --> 00:03:59.277
Exhausted and tired, he closed his eyes.

56
00:03:59.278 --> 00:04:05.029
When Bobby opened his eyes again, it took a moment for him to remember where he was.

57
00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:08.916
He must have fallen asleep next to Huey's well.

58
00:04:08.917 --> 00:04:15.111
"Bobby?" a familiar voice called from the distance.

59
00:04:15.112 --> 00:04:17.766
Bobby's heart skipped a beat.

60
00:04:17.767 --> 00:04:19.612
He knew that voice.

61
00:04:19.613 --> 00:04:25.352
From the trees, Cy, Panther, and Jane came running toward him.

62
00:04:25.353 --> 00:04:28.110
Bobby could not hold back his tears.

63
00:04:28.111 --> 00:04:32.845
"I'm so sorry,"

64
00:04:32.846 --> 00:04:37.305
he cried as he hugged his brother and sisters.

65
00:04:37.306 --> 00:04:41.601
They looked at him strangely, but did not say anything.

66
00:04:41.602 --> 00:04:52.739
As the sun disappeared behind the hill, Bobby was so glad to see his family again that he could have burst with happiness.

